{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305136,"nonce":"TTA84KwXfc5Sx4mW+8HUted5ka0=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhkLw","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/18","origin":"github"},"title":"--autodetect_output_dir cannot work: requires PyQt4 with QtCore.QString","message":"```python\nfrom PyQt4 import QtCore\nsettings = QtCore.QSettings(..., QtCore.QSettings.IniFormat)\nroot = settings.value(\"torrents\").toPyObject()\nrecord = root[QtCore.QString(hash)]\n```\n\nTwo independent blockers:\n\n- PyQt4 has no Python 3 build and is long unmaintained. The project migrated to Python 3 in commit `8e4c5db`, which left this path dead.\n- `QtCore.QString` does not exist in PyQt4's Python 3 API (v2 API) even where PyQt4 is available, and `.toPyObject()` likewise.\n\nSo `-a` fails at import on every supported interpreter.\n\nIt can be reimplemented with no dependency at all: modern qBittorrent stores one bencoded `.fastresume` file per torrent in `BT_backup/`, containing `save_path`. The project already has a bencode parser, so reading it needs no Qt.","files":null}]}